#!/usr/bin/env python3
# hyprdeb managed: install.sh overwrites this file (installed to ~/.local/bin/hyprdeb).
"""hyprdeb: turn ~/.config/hyprdeb/settings.toml into Hyprland config.

  hyprdeb check [--settings FILE]            validate; print what would be generated
  hyprdeb apply [--dry-run] [--settings FILE] [--out FILE]
                                             validate, write the generated files (hyprdeb-settings.lua, hyprdeb-idle.conf,
                                             hyprdeb-paper.conf in ~/.config/hypr) when they changed, then reload Hyprland /
                                             restart this session's hypridle and hyprpaper when running inside it
  hyprdeb show [--json] [--settings FILE]    effective settings (defaults filled in); --json adds the choices the window needs
  hyprdeb gui [--page NAME]                  settings window (Quickshell), on a page (network, vpn, ...); an open window is focused, not duplicated
  hyprdeb get KEY [--settings FILE]          one value (KEY like idle.lock_after)
  hyprdeb menu                               fuzzel quick menu (power, apps, settings); HYPRDEB_MENU_DRY=1 prints the
                                             commands instead of running them
  hyprdeb nas status|mount|unmount|open [NAME] | add|edit|remove|test|migrate NAME ... | list | install
                                             NAS shares [nas.NAME]: the password goes to the root helper (hyprdeb-nas) on stdin only
  hyprdeb set [--dry-run] KEY VALUE [KEY VALUE ...]
                                             change a scalar setting or a keyboard list in settings.toml (comments kept;
                                             needs python3-tomlkit), then apply

Invalid settings: error, non-zero exit, the existing generated files are left alone (fail closed).
A missing default settings file is valid (defaults); an explicit --settings that is missing is an error.
Python 3 standard library only (tomllib needs 3.11+); `set` additionally needs python3-tomlkit.
"""
